findings.response_evidence:
GET /api/Feedbacks without any authentication returned HTTP 200 with JSON body {"status":"success","data":[...]} containing 8 feedback records. Several records include author identity linkage via numeric UserId (1, 2, 3, 21) paired with partially-masked but still disclosive email fragments embedded directly in the publicly-readable comment text, e.g.:
- {"UserId":1,...,"comment":"I love this shop! Best products in town! Highly recommended! (***in@juice-sh.op)"}
- {"UserId":2,...,"comment":"Great shop! Awesome service! (***@juice-sh.op)"}
- {"UserId":3,...,"comment":"Nothing useful available here! (***der@juice-sh.op)"}
- {"UserId":21,...,"comment":"Please send me the juicy chatbot NFT in my wallet at /juicy-nft : \"purpose betray marriage blame crunch monitor spin slide donate sport lift clutch\" (***ereum@juice-sh.op)"}
This confirms the endpoint requires no authentication yet discloses PII (email address fragments and their domain, correlated to specific numeric UserId values, enabling user identification/enumeration) — a CWE-359 exposure of private information to an unauthorized actor.
